  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Public Administration in Ethiopia is showing an early but meaningful scholarly footprint, paired with substantial usage. The book has been downloaded 14,600 times through OAPEN and has 6 OpenAlex citations, suggesting that it is being read and then beginning to inform subsequent research.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">As the first handbook on Ethiopian public administration, this 2020 Leuven University Press volume addresses a practical and policy-relevant field at a time when building an effective, inclusive, and accountable state remains a major concern in Ethiopia. Its open availability appears to have supported broad reach: the record shows 14,600 downloads, indicating sustained reader interest rather than a purely archival presence.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citation record is still modest, but it is already visible. Six citing works have appeared across 2021, 2024, and 2025, with most of the recent uptake concentrated in journal articles. That pattern suggests the book is being drawn into active conversations on public administration, governance, accountability, and related reform questions, especially in Ethiopian contexts.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing landscape is also instructive. Recent references appear in venues such as Cogent Business &amp; Management, Public Administration and Development, and the Journal of Public Affairs Education, showing that the book is circulating across public administration and adjacent management and education venues. Several citing works focus on themes aligned with the handbook\u2019s scope, including meritocracy, accountability, governance competencies, organizational change, and public service reform.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Beyond citations, the record shows open repository availability and a WorldCat holding, which support discoverability and potential teaching use. There is no event archive to summarize, and the available evidence is therefore weighted toward usage and scholarly uptake rather than public-facing discourse. Overall, the book\u2019s impact profile is that of an accessible foundational reference: widely downloaded, already cited, and starting to shape subsequent empirical and comparative work on public administration in Ethiopia and beyond.</p>",
